## Model card

- **Name:** GPT-6 Luna
- **Short description:** OpenAI’s GPT-6 Luna is an efficiency-focused GPT-6 tier model for high-volume, focused tasks such as summarization and extraction, with 1.05M context and low pricing.
- **Provider / access:** OpenAI API/ChatGPT surfaces (per metadata/docs). Local metadata lists `openai/gpt-6-luna` and `noFreeId`.
- **Release / knowledge:** Developer docs list knowledge cutoff May 18, 2026. Announcement page not accessible in this pass.
- **IDs:** `gpt-6-luna`.
- **Context window:** 1,050,000 context window; 922,000 maximum input tokens; 128,000 max output tokens (OpenAI developer docs).
- **Modalities:** Text and image input; text output (OpenAI developer docs).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** $0.10 / 1M input, $0.01 / 1M cached input, $0.125 / 1M cache writes, $0.50 / 1M output (OpenAI developer docs). Prompts >272K input priced at 2x input/cache and 1.5x output for full request; Batch/Flex 50% of Standard, Fast 2x, regional processing premium applies.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary OpenAI model; architecture/parameter count not publicly disclosed.

